  "id": "Compound::DB00346 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Alfuzosin and Cyp3a4 appear to be linked through a mechanism involving the inhibition of cytochrome P450 3A4 (Cyp3a4), a key enzyme in drug metabolism. The evidence suggests that Alfuzosin may act as a causal agent for conditions such as blood pressure reduction and intraoperative floppy iris syndrome, both of which are associated with Tamsulosin or Clorazepate. These latter substances bind to Cyp3a4, implying a potential pathway where Alfuzosin could influence the activity of Cyp3a4 through some unspecified mechanism. The shared binding of Tamsulosin and Clorazepate to Cyp3a4, along with the causal relationships between Alfuzosin and these compounds, supports a plausible link between Alfuzosin and Cyp3a4, particularly in the context of drug metabolism. The low scores in the paths suggest that while the relationship is supported, the exact mechanism remains unclear, necessitating further investigation into the specific interaction between Alfuzosin and Cyp3a4.",
